Z||000001||AusFiero||05-15-2001||08:37 PM||||Yeah they would fit.<BR>Sorry though Loki. Not from me they wont  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I have never been much of a lover of overdone. Those scoopy, flat, grilled, vented god knows what you call em fronts are one of the main reasons I bought an American car. So I didn't have to have a Nissan with 37,003 scoops on it. To many like em around now and most of them are just an abortion of the original shapes, rather than an accentuation of the original shape.<P>Just my views though. I am from the old school of nice paint, tasteful body mods and detail make a car. Not look I got a vent in the front of my car big enough to fit an intercooler capable of being on the space shuttle. <BR>We have one ricer show car here. Bloke spent over a $100 K on it. It too is totally overdone. He wonders why people who own tasteful cars laugh at it at shows. If he doesn't know now he never will. This thing has vents on the inside of the doors even?? And of course the usual go faster ricer stickers. A chrome dash to "tastefully" compliment the lime green and orange interior? 20" wheels with a tyre profle so low you would have trouble with even the most basic driveway. 1" hump and smash ya rims. <BR>Personally I can't see the point of it. Does the bloke think his $100,000 plus rolling Japanese bordello is more tasteful than the used Ferarri or new Porsche Boxster he coulda bought with the money?<P>Ok..had my *****  session now. Leave rice in Japan where it belongs.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||13
